    "bodyHtml": "<h2>Direct answer</h2>\n<p>For label work, choose a foil grade as a starting point based on the label substrate and the intended process, then sample it with the finished surface and production artwork. A supplier's compatibility information can help narrow the starting options, but it does not replace a job-specific trial.</p>\n<h2>Diagnosis table</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Observation</th>\n<th>Check first</th>\n<th>Conservative next step</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Incomplete transfer</td>\n<td>Surface condition, die contact, and foil grade</td>\n<td>Compare a small set of controlled samples before changing several variables at once.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Soft or filled detail</td>\n<td>Artwork detail, die condition, and dwell</td>\n<td>Sample the production artwork and inspect the smallest required details.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uneven appearance</td>\n<td>Substrate variation, coating, and pressure distribution</td>\n<td>Keep the sample material representative of the production label.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Sampling steps</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Record the label facestock, coating or varnish, artwork detail, and machine setup used for the sample.</li>\n<li>Run a controlled sample while changing one practical variable at a time.</li>\n<li>Inspect transfer completeness, edge definition, and adhesion according to the job's agreed acceptance method.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Final settings require confirmation through sampling on the actual substrate, machine, artwork/design, and speed. Keep the approved sample and its setup record with the job information.</p>\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>What should be checked first when sampling foil for labels?</h3>\n<p>Confirm the actual label substrate and surface treatment, then review transfer completeness, edge definition, and adhesion using the production artwork and process.</p>\n<h3>Can one foil grade be assumed to suit every label material?</h3>\n<p>No. Label facestock, coatings, varnishes, inks, and process conditions can differ, so a production-representative sample is needed before final selection.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.univacco.com/hot-stamping-foil.htm\">UNIVACCO: Hot Stamping Foil</a> describes heat-and-pressure transfer and lists substrate and machine categories.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.heidelberg.com/global/en/print_and_packaging/products/offset_printing/peripherals/printing_and_coating_unit/foil_star/product_information_19/foil_star.jsp\">HEIDELBERG: Cold transfer unit FoilStar</a> describes a label-transfer configuration using adhesive, substrate, and UV curing.</li>\n</ul>\n"
